An adapter sleeve is the simplest way to mount a taper-bore bearing onto a plain cylindrical shaft. The outer surface of the sleeve is tapered to match the bearing bore while the inner surface sits on the shaft, so no shoulder, step or machined seat is required.

Tightening the lock nut draws the bearing up the taper, which expands the sleeve and grips the shaft. The mounting ends up both concentric and firmly located, and it is what allows a single shaft diameter to carry a range of bearing sizes.

Kaybee International holds ready stock of adapter sleeves across the shaft sizes most often called for in Indian industry, and supplies non-standard sizes made to requirement where equipment falls outside conventional dimensions.
